@*
    The single loading primitive for in-page regions.

    House rule (DESIGN-SYSTEM.md → "Loading"): anything that will render figures, rows or an empty
    state has to distinguish "no data yet" from "no data". A stat that shows 0 and silently becomes
    47 a second later is worse than no stat at all — the reader has already believed the 0.

    Wrap the region, pass one IsLoading that is true until EVERY store the region reads has landed
    (LoadState.UntilAll composes them), and the gate shows the pulsing jewel in the region's own
    space until the whole thing can be shown at once.

    Use it sparingly. A gate is for a REGION that will definitely render something and takes up
    real space — a table, a stat grid, a panel body. Not a filter or a picker (render those
    `disabled` with a "Loading…" placeholder), not a single line of text (just do not render it
    until the number is known), and not a panel that only exists when it has something to show
    (its absence during the load is the same as its absence after). Three of these pulsing down
    one page is worse than the zeros they replaced.

    Prominent="true" for a main panel — anything occupying roughly a third of the screen or more —
    which gets the larger jewel and a taller reserved space so the page does not jump when the
    content arrives. Overlay="true" instead keeps already-rendered content in place and floats the
    jewel over it, which is the right choice for a refresh (filters, pagination, tab switches)
    where the previous answer is still meaningful.
*@

@if (!IsLoading)
{
    @ChildContent
}
else if (Overlay)
{
    <div class="relative">
        @ChildContent
        <JewelSpinner Overlay="true" Size="@SpinnerSize" IconSize="@IconSize" Label="@Label" />
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="@MinHeight flex items-center justify-center" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
        <JewelSpinner Size="@SpinnerSize" IconSize="@IconSize" Label="@Label" Class="py-0" />
    </div>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>True until every store this region reads has produced its first result.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool IsLoading { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A main panel rather than an inline region: bigger jewel, taller reserved space.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Prominent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Float the indicator over the existing content instead of replacing it. Use when the
    /// content on screen is a previous, still-useful answer being refreshed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Overlay { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Caption under the jewel. Keep it specific — "Loading valuations" beats "Loading".</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; } = "Loading";

    /// <summary>Override the reserved height when the incoming content has a known size.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Height { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private string MinHeight => Height ?? (Prominent ? "min-h-[220px]" : "min-h-[96px]");

    private string SpinnerSize => Prominent ? "w-12 h-12" : "w-8 h-8";

    private string IconSize => Prominent ? "w-5 h-5" : "w-3.5 h-3.5";
}
